export const sample={id:'sample-digital-v1',title:'When connection becomes a necessity',subtitle:'当连接成为一种生活必需',category:'社会与科技',source:'原创六级风格练习 · 非历年真题',paragraphs:[
 'For many people, an ordinary day begins with a screen. They check the weather, pay for a journey and exchange messages before reaching the office. These habits are so familiar that digital access is often taken for granted. Yet a society that moves its essential services online can create new barriers for those who remain disconnected. The question is no longer simply whether technology makes life more convenient, but whether everyone has a fair opportunity to participate.',
 'The digital divide is frequently described as a gap between people who own devices and those who do not. This definition, however, overlooks a more complex reality. A household may possess a smartphone but struggle to afford a reliable connection. An older person may have access to the internet without the confidence to complete an online application. Meaningful access therefore depends on a combination of equipment, affordability and practical skills.',
 'The consequences extend beyond inconvenience. When job advertisements, medical appointments and public information are primarily available online, limited access can reinforce existing inequalities. People already facing economic disadvantages must devote extra time and effort to tasks that others complete in minutes. Over time, this can weaken their sense of belonging: they are physically present in a community while being excluded from some of its everyday conversations and opportunities.',
 'Providing inexpensive devices is a useful starting point, but it is unlikely to be sufficient on its own. Community libraries offer another approach. Alongside free connections, some provide patient, practical guidance from trained volunteers. Participants can learn to identify misleading information, protect their privacy and use services independently. Such support works best when it responds to individual needs instead of assuming that every learner faces the same difficulty.',
 'None of this requires abandoning digital innovation. Rather, it calls for a broader understanding of progress. A service should not be judged solely by the speed with which its most confident users can navigate it. Designers and policymakers also need to consider who may be left behind. Keeping accessible alternatives, while investing in skills and affordable connections, can ensure that efficiency and inclusion develop together. The value of connection lies in the opportunities it opens to people.'
],questions:[
 {prompt:'What does the author suggest about digital access in the first paragraph?',options:['It has made essential services less useful.','It matters mainly to people who work in offices.','It has become important for equal participation in society.','It is taken seriously by everyone.'],answer:'C',evidence:0,quote:'whether everyone has a fair opportunity to participate',explanation:'第一段由日常数字习惯转向公平参与。最后一句是主旨：问题不仅是便利性，还包括每个人是否有公平参与的机会。C 对应 fair opportunity to participate。A 无依据；B 范围过窄；D 把 taken for granted（视为理所当然）误解为认真对待。',skill:'主旨理解'},
 {prompt:'Why does the author mention a household with a smartphone?',options:['To demonstrate that all families can afford internet access.','To show that owning a device does not guarantee meaningful access.','To argue that smartphones are difficult to operate.','To explain why older people prefer online services.'],answer:'B',evidence:1,quote:'A household may possess a smartphone but struggle to afford a reliable connection.',explanation:'第二段用两个例子说明 digital divide 不只是有没有设备。家庭有手机，却可能负担不起稳定网络，直接支持 B。A 与 afford 的困难相反；C 和 D 都不是该例的目的。',skill:'例证作用'},
 {prompt:'According to paragraph 3, limited digital access may lead to what?',options:['A reduced sense of belonging in a community.','A decline in the number of medical appointments.','An increase in the quality of public information.','More opportunities for disadvantaged people.'],answer:'A',evidence:2,quote:'this can weaken their sense of belonging',explanation:'第三段明确指出 limited access 会加剧已有不平等，并削弱归属感。A 中 reduced 对应原文 weaken。B、C 原文没有说明；D 与 excluded from … opportunities 相反。',skill:'细节定位'},
 {prompt:'What makes the support provided by community libraries most effective?',options:['Replacing trained volunteers with online applications.','Offering identical lessons to every participant.','Focusing exclusively on the price of devices.','Adapting practical guidance to individual needs.'],answer:'D',evidence:3,quote:'it responds to individual needs',explanation:'第四段末句给出有效支持的条件：回应个体需求。D 是该句的同义改写。B 的 identical 与原文 instead of assuming … the same difficulty 相反。A、C 都偏离实际指导与个体差异。',skill:'同义替换'},
 {prompt:'Which statement best reflects the author’s view of digital progress?',options:['Innovation should stop until every person owns a device.','Efficiency should be pursued together with inclusion.','The fastest users should determine how services are designed.','Offline alternatives prevent the development of digital skills.'],answer:'B',evidence:4,quote:'efficiency and inclusion develop together',explanation:'最后一段并不反对创新，而是要求更广泛地理解进步，兼顾效率与包容。B 直接对应 efficiency and inclusion develop together。A 是绝对化推断；C 与不应只看熟练用户的原意相反；D 无依据。',skill:'观点态度'}]};
